  "summary": "Malicious code in certify-web (PyPI)",
  "details": "Package installs a PTH file that during every Python startup installs a NinjaOne (legitimate remote management tool) agent tied to the attacker-controlled account and ensures its persistence. As such, the attacker gains full control over the machine.\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: MALICIOUS - The campaign has clearly malicious intent, like infostealers.\n\n\nCampaign: 2026-11-certify-web\n\n\nReasons (based on the campaign):\n\n\n - rat\n\n\n - abuses-pth\n\n\n - persistence\n\n",
